#~ "`str`, default `'uniaxial'`. `uniaxial` strains one"
#~ " direction for responses such as C11/C22/C33; "
#~ "`biaxial` strains two directions to sample "
#~ "in-plane coupling and Poisson response; "
#~ "`isotropic` scales all axes equally for EOS"
#~ " or bulk-modulus sampling. Do not choose"
#~ " independent `triaxial` scans for a simple "
#~ "volume curve: the Cartesian product can become"
#~ " enormous."

